  "fault_schedule": "Union of the committed cluster, queue, history, Nexus, matching user data, QueueV2 and forwarding manifests. Includes actual equal-byte command collision across shard/queue families in both directions before and after reopen.",
  "assertions": [
    "Exact Go ShardStore payload/encoding and callback semantics cross real gRPC into Rust SlateDB.",
    "Lost completed response retries same operation identity and does not overwrite intervening state.",
    "Shard and outcomes reopen together; replay cannot bypass writer fencing.",
    "Missing Update and range mismatch preserve distinct typed errors.",
    "Stalled durability quarantines; caller timeout and admission are bounded.",
    "All integration fixtures execute only the freshly built Go owner; no Rust server fallback.",
    "All namespace MetadataStore methods execute across real gRPC into the Go SlateDB owner.",
    "Namespace rename/version/name indexes and durable outcomes update atomically; replay cannot cross operation families.",
    "Near-limit namespace records paginate within the default gRPC receive limit and replay identically.",
    "Cluster CAS has exactly one winner and reopens with same durable result.",
    "Replay cannot extend membership expiry or bypass fencing.",
    "Membership filters preserve strict time boundaries, optional filter presence and paging.",
    "Real gRPC and upstream manager receive byte-bounded pages and typed errors.",
    "All legacy Queue methods cross actual RPC to Go SlateDB owner.",
    "Normal and DLQ versions guard writes and Init preserves existing metadata.",
    "Lost completed response retries exact operation identity without duplicate enqueue.",
    "Message allocation survives delete-all and reopen; replay does not recreate deleted messages.",
    "Aborted transaction publishes neither staged delete nor outcome journal.",
    "Queue replay rejects fenced owners.",
    "Near-limit page fits default gRPC response bound and continuation omits no record.",
    "All seven history methods cross actual gRPC to the Go native owner.",
    "Forward and reverse multipage reads return complete node/transaction sequences; metadata-only preserves ordering.",
    "Exact-key append uses PostgreSQL upsert semantics.",
    "New branch/tree/node abort together; acknowledged tree and nodes reopen together with durable replay.",
    "Fork and deletion boundaries preserve ancestry guard and opaque tree information.",
    "Lost completed append response retries unchanged identity; fenced owner cannot replay.",
    "Bounded large-node pagination preserves continuation; append timeout types match selected SQL paths.",
    "Endpoint and catalog version CAS commit atomically, failed CAS and missing delete leave catalog unchanged.",
    "Reopen preserves endpoint bytes, versions and historical outcomes; changed replay is rejected and a competing owner fences replay.",
    "Five 1MiB endpoints page completely in binary UUID order within 3MiB responses.",
    "Actual gRPC preserves blobs, retries a lost completed response once without a second mutation, and returns observed catalog version with stale-list errors.",
    "Eight legacy matching queue/tasks operations cross real Go adapter gRPC into the official native SlateDB owner.",
    "Stale range and duplicate batches leave no partial writes across subqueues.",
    "Sorted bounded task pages, completion limits, and byte-bounded queue/task pages preserve blobs.",
    "Completed-response retry and reopened outcome replay preserve state and identity.",
    "Full pinned legacy TaskStore satisfies upstream TaskQueue, TaskQueueTask and TaskQueueUserData suites over actual gRPC.",
    "Namespace batches atomically update user-data versions and build-ID mappings; pointer Applied/Conflicting outputs survive typed transport.",
    "Conflict and duplicate mapping rollback preserve both data and indexes; durable replay/reopen cannot repeat prior mutation.",
    "User-data near-limit pages preserve three complete blobs across byte-budget continuation.",
    "Pinned upstream QueueV2 and HistoryTaskQueueManager interface suites pass over real gRPC.",
    "Range-delete metadata and messages commit atomically; replay preserves subsequent enqueue.",
    "Pages obey full3MiB wire budget and exact protobuf continuation format.",
    "Terminal and stale cursors cannot wrap or resurrect logically deleted sentinel.",
    "Complete operation envelope unchanged across actual gRPC forwarding.",
    "Stale route refresh reaches owner; in-memory recorded response prevents a second logical test execution.",
    "Router retains the incoming context deadline without creating a fresh timeout; caller cancellation reaches the forwarded destination.",
    "Cycles and invalid hop counts fail within bounded attempts; missing deadline rejected; stalled local call respects deadline.",
    "Closed router rejects new local admissions.",
    "Equal command bytes in different RPC families cannot replay another family outcome.",
    "Native matching range seeks preserve signed bounds and exclusive cursor endpoints without rescanning prior rows."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Single logical partition; no directory/routing/full Temporal boot.",
    "Memory object store only; no real-S3 or process-crash recovery claim.",
    "Native registered proof; pinned container orchestration remains a separate shipping gate.",
    "Memory object store; no process-crash or real S3 claim.",
    "Legacy Queue and QueueV2 are covered; full Temporal boot remains pending.",
    "Three pinned SQL deviations explicitly adjudicated in issue30 and contract evidence.",
    "Memory object store only; no S3/process-crash proof.",
    "History component only, not full ExecutionStore or Temporal boot.",
    "GetAllHistoryTreeBranches covers configured partition; adapter routing/global fanout remains a later gate.",
    "Pinned PostgreSQL reverse and metadata-only query defects corrected explicitly; no broad SQL parity claim.",
    "Local memory object store only, no real S3/Temporal boot/FairTaskStore/distributed catalog proof.",
    "Blob1MiB, command1800KiB, batch/list1000, response3MiB ceilings remain; nonpaginated build-ID result fails explicitly above budget.",
    "Upstream suites generate randomized UUIDs/task IDs in pinned code; workload shape fixed, not byte-identical generated inputs. Custom fault fixtures use committed IDs.",
    "Upstream conformance helper uses declared1ms WAL flush for1024durable one-row reads inside upstream30s deadline. Production default remains100ms; every operation still awaits durability.",
    "Transport component only; test resolver and recorded response are in-memory fixtures, not S3 authority or durable replay proof.",
    "Production ownership manager, process integration and live scale-out remain required."
  ],
